      "q": "14. Show that the point $A(1,2,3),B( - 1, - 2, - 1),C(2,3,2)$ and $D(4,7,6)$ taken in order form the vertices of a parallelogram. Do these form a rectangle?",
      "a": "Mid-point of\n$AC$\nis\n$\\left( {\\dfrac{{1 + 2}}{2},\\dfrac{{2 + 3}}{2},\\dfrac{{3 + 2}}{2}} \\right)$\ni.e.\n$\\left( {\\dfrac{3}{2},\\dfrac{5}{2},\\dfrac{5}{2}} \\right)$\nalso the mid-point of\n$BD$\nis\n$\\left( {\\dfrac{{ - 1 + 4}}{2},\\dfrac{{ - 2 + 7}}{2},\\dfrac{{ - 1 + 6}}{2}} \\right)$\ni.e.\n$\\left( {\\dfrac{3}{2},\\dfrac{5}{2},\\dfrac{5}{2}} \\right)$\nThen\n$AC$\nand\n$BD$\nhave same mid-points\n$\\therefore $$AC$\nand\n$BD$\nbisect each other , It is a Parallelogram.\nNow\n$AC = \\sqrt {{{(2 - 1)}^2} + {{(3 - 2)}^2} + {{(2 - 3)}^2}}\u00a0 = \\sqrt 3 $\nand\n$BD = \\sqrt {{{(4 + 1)}^2} + {{(7 + 2)}^2} + {{(6 + 1)}^2}}\u00a0 = \\sqrt {155} $\n$\\therefore AC \\ne BD$\ndiagonals are not equal\nPQRS is not a rectangle."
