      "a": "let the point\n$C$\ndivide the line segment joining the point\n$A$\nand\n$B$\nin the ratio\n$\\lambda\u00a0 = 1$\n, Then co-ordinates of Point\n${\\text{R}}$\n$\\left[ {\\dfrac{{8\\lambda\u00a0 + 2}}{{\\lambda\u00a0 + 1}},\\dfrac{{ - 3}}{{\\lambda\u00a0 + 1}},\\dfrac{{10\\lambda\u00a0 + 4}}{{\\lambda\u00a0 + 1}}} \\right]$\nThe\n$x$\nco-ordinates of point\n$C$\nis 4\n$ \\Rightarrow \\dfrac{{8\\lambda\u00a0 + 2}}{{\\lambda\u00a0 + 1}} = 4 = \\lambda\u00a0 = \\dfrac{1}{2}$\n$\\therefore $\nco-ordinates of point\n${\\text{R}}$\n$\\left[ {4,\\dfrac{{ - 3}}{{\\dfrac{1}{2} + 1}} \\cdot \\dfrac{{10 \\times \\dfrac{1}{2} + 4}}{{\\dfrac{1}{2} + 1}}} \\right]$\ni.e.\n$(4, - 2,6)$"
