      "q": "16. If the points $A(1,0, - 6) = B( - 3,P,q)$ and $C( - 5,9,6)$are collinear, find the values of ${\\mathbf{P}}$and ${\\mathbf{q}}$",
      "a": "Given points\n$A(1,0, - 6) = B( - 3,P,q)$\nand\n$C( - 5,9,6)$\nare collinear\nLet point\n$B$\ndivide\n$AC$\nin the ratio K:1\n$\\therefore $\nco-ordinates of point\n$A\\left( {\\dfrac{{1 - 5K}}{{K + 1}} \\cdot \\dfrac{{0 + 9K}}{{K + 1}},\\dfrac{{ - 6 + 6K}}{{K + 1}}} \\right)$\n$B( - 3,P,q)$\n$\\dfrac{{1 - 5K}}{{K + 1}} =\u00a0 - 3$\n$1 - 5K =\u00a0 - 3K - 3$\n$ - 2K =\u00a0 - 4$\n$K = \\dfrac{{ - 4}}{{ - 2}}$\n$K = 2$\n$\\therefore $\nThe value of\n${\\text{P}}$\nand\n${\\text{q}}$\nare 6 and 2."
