      "q": "2. Show that the Following Points are the Vertices of an Isosceles Right-angled Triangle.\nA (7, 10), B (-2, 5) and C (3, -4)\nSolution\n: Given, the three points are A, B, and C having coordinates (7, 10), (-2, 5), and (3, -4) respectively.\nAB = \u221a (( -2 \u2013 7 )\n2\n+ ( 5 \u2013 10 )\n2\n)\n= \u221a106 units. \u2026\u2026\u2026 (1)\nBC = \u221a (( 3 + 2 )\n2\n+ ( -4 \u2013 5 )\n2\n)\n= \u221a106 units\n\u2026\u2026\u2026 (2)\nAC = \u221a (( 3 \u2013 7 )\n2\n+ ( -4 \u2013 10 )\n2\n)\n= \u221a212 units. \u2026\u2026\u2026 (3)\nFrom equations 1 and 2 we can see,\nAB = BC\u2026\u2026 (4)\nTherefore, triangle ABC is an isosceles triangle.\nAlso, AB\n2\n= 106\nBC\n2\n= 106\nAC\n2\n= 212\nWe can see that,\nAB\n2\n+ BC\n2\n= AC\n2\n\u2026\u2026. (5)\nIt is a satisfying Pythagoras Theorem.\nTherefore, triangle ABC is a right-angled triangle.\nAnd from equation 4 and 5, we can say that\nThe triangle ABC is an isosceles right-angled triangle. Hence, proved.",
